From fe19ffbe4bbc6b0e9e13c37d6387209023e62976 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bherbruck <brennen.herbruck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:34:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): the cross-drill station hop clears off-centre
 mouths

The hop plane between quarter-turn stations was sized for mouths on
their stations' centre lines; an off-centre pair's chord could dip
inside the bar (an (8,-6)/(-6,8) pair on r10 passed 10.757 mm from the
spindle) and the rapid proof refused the op. traverse_s now measures
the chord between the two real hop points and raises the plane until
it clears; on-centre pairs keep the closed-form plane exactly.

Fixes #81

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
